# Artifacts that carry a live value legitimately, one per line: the file, two spaces, the value, two
# spaces, **how many times it may appear**, two spaces, and why. Anything not recorded here fails
# generation.
#
# **The occurrence count is new with H-20 (#60), and it is the part that is enforced rather than read.**
# An exemption used to be a file and a value, so one entry blanketed every occurrence in that file: a
# second use could appear beneath it and no gate would say so. The count is the raw number of times
# the value appears in the file, comments included, because the gate compares it against the tree and
# a qualified number cannot be compared. A count that no longer matches fails and names both figures.
#
# `LIVE-VALUES.txt` carried a hand-written block of exactly these counts, for the values the list
# could not hold. Six of its rows were uses of the epoch index 20723; those epochs are listed now, so
# those rows are entries below and a person no longer has to be the one checking them.
#
# **It also found a dead entry the moment it was added.** `vectors/V-P-12.json` was exempted for the
# checkpoint address `H3ERVV7P3yNQxXXJrzVvmS2Nzh9qBd283kcAgMHzHDNn`, "the two-seed case". That address
# appears nowhere in the repository but this file and `LIVE-VALUES.txt`: the vector was regenerated at
# some point and the entry stayed. The old check asked only whether the list held the value, which it
# does, so nothing could see it. The line is gone, and a count of zero is now refused outright.
#
# **The file is its repository-relative path, exactly (H-25 review, H3).** A bare file name was
# accepted too, and one entry for `(X.json, value)` then exempted that value in every other `X.json`
# anywhere in the scanned surface. Both the generators and the tree walk now key by the artifact's
# destination in the repository, so one spelling is enough and it is the specific one.
#
# The distinction the rule draws: an artifact whose *subject* is the announced deployment may name it;
# an artifact that merely looks more concrete for carrying one may not.

vectors/V-P-12.json  By5XeTsCS4Qf17U9EuGUTzEFz29wQdFFeqJtfhnFQkZB  1  §2.4's derivation is checked against this deployment, which is the vector's whole subject
vectors/V-P-12.json  0xa2f283cb90ea20af164f791073b89f5f22f59081f8509f664721ec57df9fb7ee  1  the same program id, as the bytes the derivation hashes
vectors/V-P-12.json  CZM6LnvAX2D7FGbGwfWMCTG9rRhgzX3JjZQxTjNvRYz7  1  the address §2.4 publishes and the derivation must reproduce
vectors/V-P-12.json  0xabb9dc3b417c0d0fe2b99d109e5d1b0b8b71c7e693c20e756cabdf7e6d30d6fc  1  the same address, as bytes
vectors/V-P-12.json  0xee4d543bd97a4e39c47cf3e12e017b329fe9d1b5bd0ee7bb9942f98206bb612f  1  the same address, as the bytes the vector carries
ts/test/units.test.ts  By5XeTsCS4Qf17U9EuGUTzEFz29wQdFFeqJtfhnFQkZB  1  §2.4's derivation checked against the announced deployment, which is this test's subject (H-25)
ts/test/units.test.ts  CZM6LnvAX2D7FGbGwfWMCTG9rRhgzX3JjZQxTjNvRYz7  1  the address that derivation must reproduce, and the reason the test is worth running (H-25)

# The two placeholder constants the 24 September deployment holds (review of PR #121, H-01).
# These travelled out of the repository, not into it: `tests/devnet.rs` published them to a
# throwaway program, and every file below predates that. The rule stays unqualified — both are
# listed, so a *new* artifact reaching for either still fails generation — and the files that
# legitimately hold them are named here by exact path. Narrowing the rule to exclude values the
# repository authored is the owner's call, not a tool's.

# V-P-13 carries `ASSESSMENT_DIGEST`, `[0x33; 32]` (H-04). It postdates the 24 September
# publication, unlike the entries above, but the direction of travel is the same and is what
# matters: this is a generator constant a harness sent to a throwaway program, not a value borrowed
# from it.
#
# Every future record vector will need a line like this. H-45 (#137) records that cost.

# **Epoch day indices (H-20, #60).** Listed since 21 October 2026, so these uses are exempted here
# rather than recorded in a comment for a reader to check. Twelve of the twenty-seven uses in the
# synthetic surface are artifacts whose subject really is the announced deployment; the other fifteen
# were synthetic artifacts that had borrowed a real date, and those values were changed instead.

demo/app.js  20723  1  Scene 1 rebuilds the announced log's first epoch, which is the scene's subject
demo/fixtures/root.json  20723  1  the committed root fixture for that scene
demo/fixtures/disclosure.json  20723  1  the package the scene verifies, same epoch
demo/fixtures/tampered.json  20723  1  the altered copy of that package
demo/test/footprint.test.mjs  20723  5  the scene's own account and two instructions, plus the comment explaining why the slot that used to sit beside them is gone
vectors/V-P-12.json  20723  2  §2.4's derivation is checked against this deployment's epoch-20723 checkpoint, which is the vector's whole subject
crates/certimining-client/tests/program_addresses.rs  20723  1  the same derivation through Solana's own find_program_address, spelled `20_723`, which is this file's whole subject
crates/certimining-client/tests/publish_epoch.rs  20723  1  the range of the announced log's epochs this harness built, recorded in prose
crates/certimining-client/tests/publish_epoch.rs  20730  1  the other end of that range, same sentence
benches/src/lib.rs  20728  1  the epoch whose published root this benchmark's figures are compared against
programs/certimining-checkpoint/tests/compute.rs  20727  1  the attachment whose measured compute units this harness is checked against
programs/certimining-checkpoint/tests/compute.rs  20728  1  the publication whose measured compute units this harness is checked against
